            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Pre-Cold Start Creative Planning Checklist</h2>
<p>Before launching a new product, creative preparation directly determines cold start success. Confirm each item below before launching ads:</p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] <strong>Product USP Mapping</strong>: List 3-5 core selling points, prioritizing those with strong visual potential (e.g., design, use cases, before/after comparisons)</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Competitor Creative Research</strong>: Search relevant keywords on TikTok, save 20-30 high-view videos, and document popular script structures</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Target Audience Profiling</strong>: Define initial countries/regions, age targeting, and interest tag combinations</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Budget Allocation Plan</strong>: Recommend allocating no more than 30% of total budget for week-one testing to preserve iteration capacity</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Creative Specs Confirmation</strong>: Vertical 9:16 (1080x1920) as the primary format, with cover images prepared separately</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>A utility app team in Southeast Asia completed their first-week testing with only 12 creatives, achieving a CPM under $4.2 by quickly eliminating low-performing content.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Creative Categorization and Production Cadence</h2>
<p>Your creative pool needs layered management to avoid resource waste. Build using this structure:</p>
<h3>Layer 1: Traffic-Driving Creatives (40% allocation)</h3>
<p>These aim to attract clicks, requiring visual impact or emotional hooks within 3 seconds.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Creative Type</th>
<th>Recommended Duration</th>
<th>Best For</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Pain Point Hook</td>
<td>15-30 seconds</td>
<td>Functional products, before/after demonstrations</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Scene Recreation</td>
<td>20-45 seconds</td>
<td>Lifestyle products, authentic usage scenarios</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Suspense Builder</td>
<td>10-20 seconds</td>
<td>High-interest products, comment-driving cliffhangers</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Layer 2: Trust-Building Creatives (35% allocation)</h3>
<p>Used to establish product credibility, suitable for users who've seen initial exposure.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Unboxing videos</strong>: Showcasing packaging details and product quality</li>
<li><strong>Real user testimonials</strong>: Authentic voiceovers or chat screenshots (with permission)</li>
<li><strong>Factory/brand story</strong>: Ideal for sellers with supply chain advantages</li>
</ul>
<h3>Layer 3: Conversion Creatives (25% allocation)</h3>
<p>Directly drive purchase decisions, suitable for traffic conversion phases.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Limited-time offers</strong>: With countdown subtitles</li>
<li><strong>Scarcity signals</strong>: Such as "Only 50 left"</li>
<li><strong>Clear CTAs</strong>: Straightforward purchase paths reducing user decision friction</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Creative Testing and Iteration Checklist</h2>
<h3>Testing Phase Execution Steps</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Intensive Upload Period</strong> (Days 1-3): Upload 10-15 new creatives daily, observe baseline view counts</li>
<li><strong>Data Observation Period</strong> (Days 4-7): Pause creatives with under 500 views and CTR below 1%</li>
<li><strong>Model Calibration Period</strong> (Days 8-14): Concentrate budget on Top 3 creatives, test different audience combinations</li>
<li><strong>Stable Scaling Period</strong> (Day 15+): Preserve consistently performing creatives, lock in successful ad strategies</li>
</ol>
<h3>Key Performance Thresholds</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Metric</th>
<th>Acceptable</th>
<th>Strong</th>
<th>Needs Optimization</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>3-second retention rate</td>
<td>≥30%</td>
<td>≥45%</td>
<td>&lt;25%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Engagement rate</td>
<td>≥3%</td>
<td>≥6%</td>
<td>&lt;2%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Click-through rate (CTR)</td>
<td>≥1%</td>
<td>≥2%</td>
<td>&lt;0.8%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Cost per acquisition (CPA)</td>
<td>≤20% of target LTV</td>
<td>≤15%</td>
<td>&gt;25%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Iteration Review Questions</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Which script structures delivered the lowest CPA?</li>
<li>[ ] What are the most frequently mentioned user needs in comments?</li>
<li>[ ] What new trends in competitor creatives can be adapted?</li>
<li>[ ] Are there significant creative performance differences across markets?</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Viral Creative Repurposing Strategies</h2>
<p>When a creative achieves positive ROI, don't discard it. Extend its lifecycle with these approaches:</p>
<p><strong>Localization Adaptation</strong>: Swap subtitles, background music, and accent versions for rapid market-specific replication</p>
<p><strong>Element Recombination</strong>: Extract highlight clips, re-edit with new openings or endings, creating "series" content</p>
<p><strong>UGC Secondary Creation</strong>: Encourage users to create derivative content based on original pieces, using challenge hashtags to boost organic reach</p>
<p><strong>Paid + Organic Synergy</strong>: Continue paid promotion of viral creatives while driving comment engagement to improve algorithm recommendations</p>
<hr />
<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<p>The essence of TikTok Shop new product cold start is rapidly validating market response with minimal samples. Your creative pool isn't about quantity—it's about clear structure and efficient iteration. Hopefully, this checklist helps your team reduce trial-and-error costs and identify effective creative directions in the first week.</p>
